.\" The macros used below are those described in groff_man(7) and
 \" groff_man_style(7).
.
.TH guile\-snarf 1 "2025-12-12" "@GUILE_VERSION@" "GNU Guile"
.
.SH NAME
guile\-snarf \- extracts the initialization actions from C source files
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY guile-snarf
.RB [ \-o
.IR OUTPUT\-FILE ]
.RI [ CPP\-ARG \fR\&.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan the output produced by invoking the C preprocessor (by default
.BR "gcc -E" )
with the given
.IR CPP\-ARG s,
extract the Guile initialization actions, and write them to standard
output or the specified
.IR OUTPUT\-FILE .

During snarfing, the pre-processor macro
.B SCM_MAGIC_SNARFER
is defined.  You can use this to avoid including snarfer output files
that don't yet exist by writing code like this:

.RS 4
.EX
  #ifndef SCM_MAGIC_SNARFER
  #include "foo.x"
  #endif
.EE
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o \ OUTPUT\-FILE
Write to
.IR OUTPUT\-FILE .
When \(dq-\(dq, write to standard output.  If there are errors during
processing,
.I OUTFILE
is deleted and the program exits with non-zero status.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CPP
Specifies the C preprocessor to invoke.  Defaults to
.BR "gcc -E" .
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.
.IR guile (1),
.IR pkg-config (1),
and for much more detail, the
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/guile/manual/html_node/index.html
Guile Reference Manual
.UE
which may also be available via
.BR info\ guile
or
.B M\-x info
in emacs.
